WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.485
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Team Player Toolkit.

00:00:12.485 --> 00:00:16.969
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:16.969 --> 00:00:19.660
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.351
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.351 --> 00:00:28.630
A team is people doing something together. Nobody does the whole thing alone.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:35.805
On a team, the job gets shared. Your part matters, and so does everyone else's.

00:00:35.805 --> 00:00:42.980
Being a team player is not about being the best. It is about helping the whole team do its best.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:47.465
Here are three tools for your toolkit.

00:00:47.465 --> 00:00:54.641
Tool one: encourage with true words. True words say what you really saw.

00:00:54.641 --> 00:01:01.816
"You kept trying." "You passed to me." "That was a hard one, and you stayed."

00:01:01.816 --> 00:01:08.095
We do not say things we do not mean. True words are the ones that help.

00:01:08.095 --> 00:01:12.579
And we name the effort, not just the ending. Effort is the part we control.

00:01:12.579 --> 00:01:19.755
Tool two: share the job. Pass the ball. Pass the crayons. Pass the turn.

00:01:19.755 --> 00:01:26.930
If someone has no part yet, that is the first job: find them one.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:32.312
A team where everyone has a part is a stronger team.

00:01:32.312 --> 00:01:39.487
Tool three: win kindly, and lose kindly. Both will happen. To everyone.

00:01:39.487 --> 00:01:46.663
Win kindly: be glad without making anyone small. "Good game" says it all.

00:01:46.663 --> 00:01:53.838
Lose kindly: it can sting a little, and that is okay. "Good game" works then, too.

00:01:53.838 --> 00:02:00.117
The game ends. The people stay. We treat people like they stay.

00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:04.602
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:04.602 --> 00:02:08.189
Eyes open. Look around your classroom. You're ready for what's next.
